Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.07,0:00:03.64,Default,,0,0,0,,TwinSleuth is a browser-based\Ntroubleshooting simulator for maintenance
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.69,0:00:08.37,Default,,0,0,0,,learners. It teaches you to predict, test\Nwithin a budget, compare evidence,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.42,0:00:10.62,Default,,0,0,0,,and defend a diagnosis instead of\Nguessing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.04,0:00:16.74,Default,,0,0,0,,This case begins with a simulated robot\Narm that refuses a PIN command
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.79,0:00:21.09,Default,,0,0,0,,before motion. The learner sees four\Npossible causes and thirty maintenance
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.14,0:00:25.37,Default,,0,0,0,,minutes. Each possible cause points to a\Ndifferent subsystem and a testable
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.44,0:00:30.60,Default,,0,0,0,,failure mode. The exercise rewards a\Ntestable explanation, not a fast guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.05,0:00:39.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}I begin with P1, repeating the same PIN\Nmotion, and commit a forecast for
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.82,0:00:44.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}each cause before observing anything. Here\Nevery row predicts refusal.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.47,0:00:47.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}Because that result would not distinguish\Nthe causes, the deterministic
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.92,0:00:52.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}Skeptic asks me to reconsider the test. It\Nuses my submitted forecast and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.55,0:00:55.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}current public state; it does not need the\Nhidden fault to raise that
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.75,0:01:00.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}question. I switch to P3 and predict that\Nkey three completes under H1 and
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.34,0:01:06.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}H4, but is refused under H2 and H3. This\Nsplits the four explanations into
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.16,0:01:10.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}two groups. Only after I commit those\Npredictions do I run the five-minute
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.09,0:01:15.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}test. The observed completion leaves two\Nmodel-consistent causes, H1 and H4.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.09,0:01:21.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}Now I test the remaining ambiguity with\NP4, the slow J2 range check. I
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.17,0:01:25.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}forecast a stop at 95 degrees for H1 and\Nfull range for the alternatives,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.97,0:01:30.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}then run it for ten simulated minutes. The\Nobservation is a J2 stop at 95
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.97,0:01:35.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}degrees. The cause list narrows to H1. The\Nledger pairs each forecast with
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.89,0:01:40.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}its observation, so I can check what\Nchanged. A test is useful when possible
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.17,0:01:44.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}causes predict different outcomes. P1\Nspent five minutes without separating
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.70,0:01:49.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}causes. P3 split the four causes into two\Npairs; P4 distinguished the two
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.90,0:01:55.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}survivors. This is the skill TwinSleuth\Npractices: choose informative tests,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.17,0:01:58.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(95,780)}update from evidence, and explain why one\Ndiagnosis remains.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.07,0:02:14.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(1500,850)}I lock H1 and cite observations for each\Nof the four causes. Getting the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.27,0:02:18.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(1500,850)}diagnosis right is not enough; I have to\Nshow evidence for each claim. The
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.79,0:02:23.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(1500,850)}debrief checks those claims instead of\Naccepting the explanation as fact. It
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.24,0:02:27.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(1500,850)}shows the five score categories\Nseparately, the remaining cause after each
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.12,0:02:31.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(1500,850)}test, and the path cost. Each claim points\Nto an event and says whether it
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.05,0:02:35.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(1500,850)}supports or contradicts a cause. The\Ndetail rows show each observation ID,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.85,0:02:40.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(1500,850)}learner belief, and evaluator status,\Nmaking every claim traceable. P4's
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.66,0:02:47.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(1500,850)}stop supports H1 and contradicts H2, H3,\Nand H4; P3 left H1 and H4 in play.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.17,0:02:52.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(1500,850)}Optional Examiner notes cannot change the\Nrubric score. Here, the two tests
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.02,0:02:56.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(1500,850)}cost fifteen minutes, matching the best\Nfeasible policy branch for this
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.77,0:03:01.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(1500,850)}simulated fault. That comparison is\Nspecific to this authored case, not a
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.36,0:03:03.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(1500,850)}real-world maintenance recommendation.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.04,0:03:09.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Behind the screen, deterministic rules\Nkeep the exercise fair. The browser
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.49,0:03:13.47,Default,,0,0,0,,sends a forecast or test choice to the\Nservice. The service enforces the run
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.52,0:03:17.79,Default,,0,0,0,,rules and time budget; the deterministic\Nengine uses the private case model
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.87,0:03:22.09,Default,,0,0,0,,to calculate the outcome and remaining\Ncauses. You see evidence only after
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.14,0:03:26.62,Default,,0,0,0,,running a test. The event ledger records\Nforecasts and outcomes in order, so
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.64,0:03:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,the session can be replayed and checked.\NThink of the rules as a referee and
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.42,0:03:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,the ledger as an instant replay: they show\Nwhat you predicted, which test
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.02,0:03:37.75,Default,,0,0,0,,you chose, and what evidence changed your\Nmind. The Skeptic sees your
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.80,0:03:41.95,Default,,0,0,0,,predictions and public information. It can\Nchallenge a weak test but cannot
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.00,0:03:46.65,Default,,0,0,0,,reveal the answer. After diagnosis,\Noptional Examiner feedback acts like a
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.65,0:03:50.88,Default,,0,0,0,,coach: it explains your evidence claims\Nbut never changes your score. This
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.93,0:03:55.33,Default,,0,0,0,,keeps the learner's reasoning—not AI\Nguesswork—at the center. The local
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.38,0:03:59.43,Default,,0,0,0,,practice still works without an AI\Nprovider. Reviewing the replay shows
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.48,0:04:02.98,Default,,0,0,0,,whether your tests separated causes and\Nhow new evidence changed your
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.03,0:04:07.75,Default,,0,0,0,,diagnosis. The experience is a simulator;\Nit is not connected to real
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.80,0:04:08.28,Default,,0,0,0,,equipment.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.04,0:04:13.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Why does the budget matter? It trains you\Nto trade time for information:
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.82,0:04:16.82,Default,,0,0,0,,choose tests that separate causes and\Navoid spending minutes on
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.87,0:04:21.57,Default,,0,0,0,,uninformative probes. In this local build,\Ncase validation, sixty-four unit
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.62,0:04:25.76,Default,,0,0,0,,tests, and fourteen browser tests passed.\NAccessibility checks include
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.81,0:04:30.06,Default,,0,0,0,,keyboard and responsive use. That gives\Nconfidence in the simulator, not
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.14,0:04:30.89,Default,,0,0,0,,real equipment.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.07,0:04:43.49,Default,,0,0,0,,TwinSleuth is a local troubleshooting\Npractice website for maintenance
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.54,0:04:48.14,Default,,0,0,0,,learners. It teaches you to predict first,\Nspend tests deliberately, compare
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.19,0:04:52.37,Default,,0,0,0,,evidence, and defend a diagnosis. The goal\Nis to improve how you investigate
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.37,0:04:57.87,Default,,0,0,0,,a fault, not memorize an answer. This is a\Nsimulator; no real equipment is
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.92,0:04:58.45,Default,,0,0,0,,connected.
